  "content": "<div id=\"readability-page-1\" class=\"page\"><div data-widget-type=\"contentparsed\" id=\"content\">\n<section>\n<div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"article-body\">\n\n<p id=\"elk-1fd0f8f2-9a41-11f1-8d16-3548496f54ff\">We're officially in dire straits. There's almost no way, if you're reading this site, that you aren't aware that memory prices have become <a data-analytics-id=\"inline-link\" href=\"https://www.tomshardware.com/pc-components/ram/one-year-into-the-ai-induced-ram-apocalypse-how-much-does-memory-actually-cost-and-is-there-hope-for-a-more-affordable-future\" target=\"_blank\" data-url=\"https://www.tomshardware.com/pc-components/ram/one-year-into-the-ai-induced-ram-apocalypse-how-much-does-memory-actually-cost-and-is-there-hope-for-a-more-affordable-future\" data-hl-processed=\"none\" data-article-category=\"pc-components\" data-mrf-recirculation=\"inline-link\" data-before-rewrite-localise=\"https://www.tomshardware.com/pc-components/ram/one-year-into-the-ai-induced-ram-apocalypse-how-much-does-memory-actually-cost-and-is-there-hope-for-a-more-affordable-future\">entirely divorced from reality</a>. Some are calling it the RAMpocalypse; I prefer \"RAMageddon.\" Whatever you want to call it, though, the reality for PC builders right now is just grim. To put this in perspective, just take a look at our <a data-analytics-id=\"inline-link\" href=\"https://www.tomshardware.com/pc-components/ram/ram-price-index-2026-lowest-price-on-ddr5-and-ddr4-memory-of-all-capacities\" target=\"_blank\" data-url=\"https://www.tomshardware.com/pc-components/ram/ram-price-index-2026-lowest-price-on-ddr5-and-ddr4-memory-of-all-capacities\" data-hl-processed=\"none\" data-article-category=\"pc-components\" data-mrf-recirculation=\"inline-link\" data-before-rewrite-localise=\"https://www.tomshardware.com/pc-components/ram/ram-price-index-2026-lowest-price-on-ddr5-and-ddr4-memory-of-all-capacities\">RAM price tracking post</a>:</p><div data-component-name=\"Slice:Table\" id=\